    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`tsgo` crashes when enabling linked editing range via `vim.lsp.linked_editing_range.enable(true)` and the server is enabled / started from a buffer whose filetype doesn't match tsgo's config.\n\nNote: **also affects Typescript 7's official LSP.**\n\nRelated: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/36646 (kind of?)\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\n- repro.lua\n\n```lua\nvim.lsp.linked_editing_range.enable(true)\n\nvim.lsp.config('tsgo', {\n    cmd = { \"/path/to/tsgo\", \"--lsp\", \"--stdio\" },\n    filetypes = { 'typescript', },\n    root_markers = { 'pnpm-lock.yaml' },\n})\n\nvim.lsp.enable('tsgo')\n```\n\n- steps\n1. `nvim --clean -u repro.lua -o pnpm-lock.yaml some-ts-file.ts` (**note:** the order is important here, the non typescript file must come first)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nserver does not crash\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1006+g31ad7d4527\n\n### Language server name/version\n\ntsgo 7.0.0-dev.20260630.1\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.1.4\n\n### Log file\n\n_No response_",
