            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> it is using the current buffer instead of the attached buffer\n\nKind of.\n\nThis resolves the issue:\n\n```patch\ndiff --git a/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/linked_editing_range.lua b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/linked_editing_range.lua\nindex 96d5c96646..4fd01467e8 100644\n--- a/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/linked_editing_range.lua\n+++ b/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/linked_editing_range.lua\n@@ -158,7 +158,15 @@ function LinkedEditor:refresh()\n     type = 'pending',\n   })\n   lsp.buf_request(bufnr, method, function(client)\n-    return util.make_position_params(0, client.offset_encoding)\n+    local winnr = 0\n+    for _, win in ipairs(api.nvim_list_wins()) do\n+      local buf = api.nvim_win_get_buf(win)\n+      if buf == bufnr then\n+        winnr = win\n+        break\n+      end\n+    end\n+    return util.make_position_params(winnr, client.offset_encoding)\n   end, function(...)\n     self:handler(...)\n   end)\n```\n\nSurely, there's a more idiomatic way to achieve this. \n\nThoughts, @ribru17?",
