        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "It seems fine for `refresh()` to assume the current window, because it is dispatched on TextChanged and CursorMoved autocmds https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/6d5b774362e9d9b586280c723060813ed7ca8757/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/linked_editing_range.lua#L171-L181.\n\nThe issue is that `on_attach()` also calls `refresh()` to get initial highlighting. But IIUC linked_editing_range side effects are only useful in the current buffer, so we can just skip the call if attached buffer is not the current?",
